competitor: Competitor name
competitorUrl: https://example.com/
audience: both
title: Unique page title no longer than 60 characters
description: Unique description between 120 and 160 characters explaining the decision this comparison resolves for the intended reader.
headline: Buddy vs Competitor for a specific decision
tagline: A concise, competitor-specific summary of the choice this page helps the reader make.
targetQueries:
  - primary non-brand comparison query
  - secondary alternative query
lastVerified: 2026-07-20
lastUpdated: 2026-07-20
faqs:
  - question: A real competitor-specific question?
    answer: A complete researched answer of at least forty characters that will appear visibly on the page.
  - question: A second decision-changing question?
    answer: Another complete answer based on this competitor rather than a reusable generic response.
  - question: Who should choose the competitor instead?
    answer: An honest answer explaining a workflow in which the competitor is the stronger choice.

# Choose 3-6 unique section types in the order this competitor's argument needs.
# Exactly one section must have type: decision. No other type is mandatory.
# Supported types: prose, snapshot, decision-factors, workflow, comparison-table,
# test-results, pricing, decision.
# Do not use evidence or limitations on sales compare pages; put honesty in choose-if and FAQs.
# See design/research/compare-pages-architecture.md.
sections: []

relatedCompares: []
